Z||000000||PTW87GT||11-08-2000||01:28 PM||||Lets say that I wanted to drive my 87GT on the reace track and many the vacuum line, canister and other emmission control stuff was old and leaky.  What could I remove without affecting performance of the MFI unit, etc.?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-09-2000||07:57 PM||||I believe you can remove all of that crap except for the vac line to the fuel pressure regulator, and the MAP sensor. You will need to ground the Park/Neutral input for the ECM to prevent the service engine light from coming on. This works for TPI V8s, and should also work for the 2.8 MPFI. The engine will run fine without the vacuum canister and EGR system.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||12
